# 3. GitLab Pipeline Trigger Policy

CRITICAL REQUIREMENT: MANUAL PIPELINE CREATION ONLY.

The pipeline must only be created when an authorized user explicitly clicks New Pipeline / Run Pipeline in the GitLab UI.

Do not automatically create pipelines for:

- Git push.
- Merge requests.
- Tag creation.
- Scheduled pipelines.
- API triggers.
- Trigger tokens.
- Parent or child pipelines.
- Upstream or downstream pipelines.
- Any other non-UI pipeline source.

Use top-level workflow rules:

```yaml
workflow:
  rules:
    - if: '$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == "web"'
      when: always
    - when: never
```

Do not use `when: manual` on every job to implement manual-only pipeline creation.

Once the user starts the pipeline through the GitLab UI, jobs should execute automatically according to their dependencies.

Do not introduce additional manual approval steps unless explicitly requested.

Ensure included templates and job-level rules do not accidentally exclude jobs from an allowed UI-created pipeline.

The pipeline must fail to create for disallowed sources.

Note that workflow rules do not independently enforce user authorization. Document any required GitLab permissions or protected-ref settings.

